4. FONT FAMILY

The font family selector must update:

design.fontFamily

Example:

User selects:

Roboto

State becomes:

design.fontFamily = "Roboto"

Then sample-preview must contain:

"fontFamily": "Roboto"

Do not send a display label if the backend expects an enum/value.

Use the exact value expected by the backend/template renderer.

When the preview is returned, the generated HTML must use the selected font.

Do not merely change the font of the React designer UI.

The invoice inside the iframe must change.

==================================================
5. FONT SIZE

Font size must be a NUMBER.

Example:

design.fontSize = 14

NOT:

design.fontSize = "14px"

NOT:

design.fontSize = "14"

The UI may display:

14 px

but the API payload must contain:

"fontSize": 14

Test multiple values:

10
12
14
16
18
20

Each must generate a visibly different invoice preview.

Do not clamp or overwrite the value unless the backend explicitly defines a valid range.

==================================================
6. FONT COLOR

Add a proper font color control if one does not already exist.

The designer should expose:

Font Color

Use a color picker/input.

Example:

design.fontColor = "#111827"

The sample-preview request MUST contain:

"fontColor": "#111827"

This value must be used by the backend-rendered invoice HTML.

Do not confuse:

fontColor

with:

primaryColor

or:

secondaryColor.

They are separate properties.

For example:

primaryColor:
controls the invoice's primary branding/theme.

secondaryColor:
controls secondary theme elements.

fontColor:
controls general invoice text.

==================================================
7. LOGO WIDTH

Make logo width a controlled numeric value.

Example:

design.logoWidth = 180

The request must contain:

"logoWidth": 180

Do not send:

"180px"

Do not store it only in CSS.

The backend must receive the numeric value.

When the user changes:

180 → 220

the preview request must change accordingly.

The rendered invoice must visibly change the logo width.

==================================================
8. LOGO HEIGHT

Same requirement for:

design.logoHeight

Example:

design.logoHeight = 60

Request:

"logoHeight": 60

Do not send:

"60px"

The backend/template renderer can convert the numeric value to the appropriate CSS unit.

Changing:

60 → 100

must result in a visibly taller logo in the preview.

